{title: Two by Two}
{subtitle: Genesis 6:13–22; 7:1–16; 8:6–12; 9:8–17}
{key: C}
{tempo: 116}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [F] [C] | [G] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Noah built a great [F]big boat
[C]Cy[G]press wood and pitch [C]to coat
Three decks high, a door [F]in the side
[C]God [G]said, Noah, come in[C]side
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Two by two, two by [F]two
[C]Birds [G]that fly and bugs [C]that crawl
Two by two, [F]two by [C]two
[G]God took care of [C]one and all
[F]Flap your wings and [C]stomp your feet
[G]Two by two, two by [C]two
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Down came rain, the [F]clouds were [C]grey
[G]Forty nights and [C]forty days
Up went the water, [F]deep and [C]wide
[G]Noah's family safe [C]inside
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Two by two, [F]two by [C]two
[G]Birds that fly and [C]bugs that crawl
Two by two, [F]two by [C]two
[G]God took care of [C]one and all
[F]Flap your wings and [C]stomp your feet
[G]Two by two, two by [C]two
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Noah opened up the window [C]wide
[G]Sent a little dove out[C]side
[F]Back she came with an olive [C]leaf
[D7]Dry land coming, [G]what a relief
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[C]I have set my [F]bow in the [C]clouds
[G]Red and orange, yellow, [C]green and blue
Never again a [F]flood, God [C]said
That's a [G]promise made to [C]me and you
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Two by two, two by [C]two
[G]God took care of [C]one and all
{end_of_verse}
